  "notes": "KANJI: Can be written as {抱|だ}っこ.\n\nUSAGE: Functions as a noun and as a する verb (だっこする).\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- だっこする (to hold in one's arms)\n- だっこしてもらう (to be held)\n- だっこ{紐|ひも} (baby carrier)\n\nRELATED WORDS: おんぶ (piggyback, carrying on back), {抱|だ}きしめる (to hug tightly), {抱|だ}く (to hold, embrace - more formal).\n\nNOTE: Children often request だっこ when they want to be picked up and carried.",
